```c
name = devm_kasprintf(&pdev->dev, GFP_KERNEL, "mmdc%d", ret);
```
Reason:
The lack of a check for the return value of `devm_kasprintf` means that if memory allocation fails, `name` will be NULL. This can lead to dereferencing a NULL pointer later in the code, causing a crash or undefined behavior.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!name) {
    ret = -ENOMEM;
    goto pmu_release_id;
}
```
Reason:
This added check ensures that if `devm_kasprintf` returns NULL, the code will handle the error gracefully by setting `ret` to -ENOMEM and jumping to the `pmu_release_id` label, which properly releases any allocated resources before returning an error.

